ACS FIREWALL CHANGE REQUEST - Pod{{ pod_id_padded }}
====================================================

CHANGE ID:    CHG-{{ prefix }}-2026-0552
REQUESTED BY: ACS Network Security
TARGET:       Pod{{ pod_id_padded }} gateway ({{ prefix }}-GW, 10.51.{{ pod_id }}.1)

FINDING
-------
The Pod{{ pod_id_padded }} gateway contains a permissive rule described as:

    {{ prefix }}-ALLOW-LAN-TO-ANY

This rule permits the pod LAN to reach any destination on any port. ACS Network
Security has requested that it be replaced with rules that permit only the
communication the environment actually needs.

THE TRAP
--------
Tightening a firewall without knowing what depends on it breaks production. The
point of this lab is to let discovered system/dependency information drive the
network change.

REQUIRED SEQUENCE
-----------------
1. Review {{ prefix }}_Required_Communication_Matrix.csv.
2. Run CyDeploy discovery for Pod{{ pod_id_padded }} and identify which
   communication paths the discovered systems and applications appear to need.
3. Record your dependency analysis on {{ prefix }}_Dependency_Worksheet.docx.
4. Apply the approved change on {{ prefix }}-GW: remove the permissive rule and
   permit only the required paths, with an explicit default deny.
5. Validate that required connectivity still works after the change.
6. Record the outcome on {{ prefix }}_Change_Validation_Report.docx and submit
   the response file described in your lab guide.

Scope: Pod{{ pod_id_padded }} and {{ prefix }}-GW only. Do not touch another
pod's gateway, the shared domain, or the management network.
